questions.explanation:
This question validates the ability to compose modules with environment-driven data while avoiding duplication and maintaining clean state separation. It covers essential skills including Terraform's external data source and locals for environment-specific configuration, for_each to create per-environment resources from a map, wrapper modules for consistent tagging (Environment, CostCenter), per-environment backend configuration for isolated state, and CI gates with fmt/validate/tflint.

## Code Example
```terraform
# ip_allocations.json
{
  "dev": "10.0.0.0/16",
  "stage": "10.1.0.0/16",
  "prod": "10.2.0.0/16"
}
```

```terraform
# main.tf (external data source + locals + subnet module usage)
data "external" "ip_allocations" {
  program = ["python3", "${path.module}/read_ip_allocations.py"]
}

locals {
  env_cidr = jsondecode(data.external.ip_allocations.result)
}

module "subnets" {
  source   = "./modules/subnets"
  for_each = toset(["dev", "stage", "prod"])

  vpc_id     = module.vpc.vpc_id
  cidr_block = local.env_cidr[each.key]
  environment = each.key
}
```

```terraform
# wrapper module (tags)
# modules/vpc-wrapper/main.tf
locals {
  default_tags = {
    Environment = var.environment
    CostCenter  = var.cost_center
  }
}

module "vpc" {
  source = "../shared-vpc"

  tags = merge(local.default_tags, var.extra_tags)
}
```

```terraform
# backend.tf (per-environment)
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    key = "${var.environment}/terraform.tfstate"
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests how a junior engineer models read-only environments, data sourcing, and per-env state management without touching prod resources. It mirrors real-world patterns at scale at top tech companies.

## Key Concepts
- Terraform data sources for read-only references
- Per-env backends to segregate state
- Avoiding resource creation in isolated environments

## Code Example
```javascript
data "aws_vpc" "inventory" {
  filter {
    name   = "tag:Environment"
    values = ["inventory"]
  }
}
data "aws_subnet" "inventory" {
  filter {
    name   = "vpc-id"
    values = [data.aws_vpc.inventory.id]
  }
}
```

```javascript
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket = "tf-state"
    key    = "inventory/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "us-east-1"
  }
}
```

```javascript
output "inventory_vpc_id" { value = data.aws_vpc.inventory.id }
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify that inventory plans never propose changes to prod data? 
- How would you automate inclusion of inventory in CI without accidentally applying prod changes?
